{
    "background_story": "Ellianna was a young anthropologist who had spent years studying the effects of tribalization on modern societies. Born to a mixed-heritage family, she had always been fascinated by the ways in which people divided themselves into groups. Her research took her to remote corners of the world, where she witnessed firsthand the tensions between traditional tribes and the forces of globalization. As she delved deeper into her work, Ellianna began to realize that tribalization was not just a relic of the past, but a powerful force that shaped contemporary politics, social media, and even her own relationships. She became determined to use her knowledge to promote cross-cultural understanding and bridge the gaps between different groups. Ellianna's work sparked a new wave of dialogue and collaboration, inspiring others to rethink the boundaries that divided them.",
